GLib calls functions through pointers of other types: a function of one
parameter as one of two, a comparison of two parameters as one of three.
C leaves such a call undefined; the native ABIs let it pass, WebAssembly
checks a called function's type and traps.

A function that frees every element of a list or a queue called
g_list_foreach with the free function cast to a GFunc: it walks the
elements itself. The sorted insert and the sort of the lists, the sort of
the arrays and g_tree_new passed a GCompareFunc where the work is done
through a GCompareDataFunc: they pass a function of that type, which
calls the GCompareFunc it gets as its user data, and the internal
functions take the type they call. The copies of a bookmark file's lists
passed functions of one parameter as GCopyFunc: they pass functions of
that type.

Not here: gtestutils.c, whose test cases keep a test of no parameters,
or of one, as a function of a fixture and its data.

